    "narrative": "The Austin Waves face a condensed slate today, with core offensive pillars **Kyle Tucker**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** unavailable due to scheduled off-days. With **Luis Robert Jr.** remaining sidelined on the IL, our offensive production hinges on mid-tier volatility. **Jorge Polanco** anchors the active unit with a marginal 50.85 score; while his recency bias is strong, the matchup against Nola presents a difficult ceiling-capper, and we must monitor the 31% rain probability in Philadelphia, which threatens to truncate his plate appearances and jeopardize our daily efficiency targets. \n\nGiven the scarcity of stolen bases in this format, the optimizer prioritized speed-heavy profiles in the remaining slots to mitigate the lack of power from our resting stars. **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** are positioned as our primary catalysts, favored for their projected efficiency on the basepaths despite lower raw power ceilings. **Heliot Ramos** and **Jackson Merrill** remain high-leverage starts, with **Ramos** benefiting from a favorable platoon split that nudges his score into the Strong tier (68.4). **Jordan Westburg** and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** represent the most difficult bench decisions; both were narrowly excluded in favor of **Andy Pages** and **Drake Baldwin**, whose park factors and projected lineup spots offered slightly higher rWAR potential against today\u2019s specific starter profiles. We are playing for volume and SB opportunity today, accepting the risk of a lower cumulative HR floor while we await the return of **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, and **Dominic Smith** to restore our middle-of-the-order slugging integrity.",
